course: dictionary
lesson: 7294
title: Words from another language
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words come from other languages, and the sentence around them can show you what they mean. The word pirouette is a dance word, and it comes from French, the language of ballet's early history.
explain: Read the clues in this sentence: «Ballet grew up at the French court, so its steps have French names such as plié and pirouette.» The steps have French names, so pirouette is the name of a dance step. Ballet is a dance style, so you can guess that a pirouette is a move that dancers do.
explain: Now test your guess by swapping in your meaning: «She did a pirouette» becomes «She spun round on one foot». That still makes sense, so your meaning fits the sentence.
fact: A pirouette is a fast spin on one foot, often on the toes.
fact: To pirouette is a verb: it means to spin round on one foot.
fact: Ballet is a dance style, and many of its steps have French names.
fact: A double pirouette means two spins in one turn.
fact: Dancers often do pirouettes in dance and PE lessons, and in stories a pirouette can show someone spinning happily or gracefully.
exercise: «Ballet grew up at the French court, so its steps have French names such as plié and pirouette.» What is a pirouette? | *A fast spin on one foot | A long jump across the stage | A type of ballet shoe | A slow walk backwards
exercise: «Mia did a double pirouette and landed on her toes.» What does double suggest? | Two stages in one room | *Two spins in one turn | Two dancers on the stage | Twice as slow
exercise: What does the verb «to pirouette» mean? | *To spin round on one foot | To run in a straight line | To jump over a fence | To sit down quietly
test: «The girl pirouetted across the room, happy as a bird.» What does pirouetted mean? | Shouted loudly | Fell over | Walked very slowly | *Spun round on one foot
test: In «Ballet grew up at the French court, so its steps have French names», which phrase tells you the step names come from French? | steps | grew up | court | *French names
exam: «The dancer spun on her toes, a graceful pirouette.» What is a pirouette here? | A loud noise from the stage | *A fast spin on one foot | A pair of ballet shoes | A bow at the end of the dance
